From bc68b40c2f1c2f43ba870532ed8f74328b3cc1e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siyuan Feng <sealseacat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:27:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] fix(llm): YAML-selectable api_style, data-egress
 warning, metadata-only mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- LocalProvider supported api_style='openai' (LM Studio, vLLM and other
  OpenAI-compatible local servers) but LLMConfig had no such field and the
  factory never passed it, so it was unreachable from YAML. Added
  llm.api_style (ollama | openai) with validation.
- Enabling the OpenAI provider now prints an explicit warning that sampled
  column values will be sent off-machine, and where.
- New llm.send_values: false (metadata-only mode) asks the model to judge
  from the column name alone — weaker detection, zero data egress. The
  prompt says so explicitly instead of sending an empty list silently.

---
